were stale compiled copies that shadowed the .ts/.tsx sources in Vite's default
resolution order (mitigated earlier via resolve.extensions, but the files were
still tracked and still edited by hand). Zero explicit '.js' imports exist and
no hand-written .js lives under src/, so removal is safe.

Verification: scripts/check-frontend-sources.sh exits 0; tsc -b clean;
vitest 39 files / 215 tests pass (was 76/424 with duplicate .test.js twins);
vite build succeeds.

